__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.env
# Case matters here: the files on disk are HANDOFF_B8.md and friends, and the
# lowercase pattern only ever matched because Windows git defaults to
# core.ignorecase=true. On the Linux CI runner it does not, so four handoff
# files would have shown up as untracked. Both cases are listed on purpose.
*handoff*.md
HANDOFF*.md
*HANDOFF*.md

# Nothing under data/ is redistributed, wherever in the tree it sits.
# data/SOURCES.md records where each set came from and the manifests record what
# was taken from it; anyone reproducing this fetches it themselves.
#
# The rule is the whole directory rather than a list of directories, for two
# reasons that were measured rather than assumed. Some of what is on disk is not
# ours to hand on: an exchange's workbooks belong to the exchange, and the copies
# here carry in their document properties the names of the people who saved them,
# which the parsed numbers never show. And a rule that names today's directories
# guards nothing tomorrow: a station opening data/b43 would have had no rule at
# all. Counted on 2026-09-04, the earlier rules let 1,519 files and 338 MB
# through, including 330 MB in a single directory and scraped pages from a
# third-party site. The rule below lets 64 through, and none of them is data.
#
# Files already tracked are unaffected: an ignore rule does not untrack anything,
# which was checked by asking git rather than by reasoning about it.
data/**

# The four exceptions are code and provenance, not data.
#
# Retrieval scripts are source that happens to live beside its output.
!data/*.py
# The templates are inputs those scripts read, with the keys stripped out.
!data/*.template.json
# The other json files at the top of data/ are the same class: each one is a
# choice pinned by hand and each carries its own _note or _comment saying which
# raw listing it was pinned against and what was measured to settle it. Which
# series, which variables, which regime is in force on which date, which page
# carries which province. Nothing retrieved is written here, and the convention
# that keeps this rule honest is that retrieved data goes in a subdirectory and
# never at the top of data/.
!data/*.json
# The three gaokao files are this project's own collection and arrangement, so
# all three are committed. The filing scores underneath are facts and belong to
# nobody; what these files are is which pages were found, which were fetched,
# which were thrown out and on what test, and how the rows were read. That work
# is recorded in data/SOURCES.md rather than asserted: twenty-four duplicate
# pages dropped by content hash, five with no article body, three excluded by
# their own headline, and two independent outlets agreeing on all 80 shared
# entries. gaokao_sources.json is the retrieval list, gaokao_provincial.csv the
# 6,386-row panel, gaokao_cutoffs.csv the 181-row per-institution reading.
!data/gaokao_cutoffs.csv
!data/gaokao_provincial.csv
# SOURCES.md is load-bearing: every file's origin URL, download date and
# definition, and different definitions never share a column.
!data/SOURCES.md
# Each manifest records, per file, the exact URL queried, the timestamp, the
# window, and how many rows were kept and dropped and why. It is the one part of
# the retrieval a reader cannot reconstruct after the fact, and all twenty come
# to under two megabytes.
!data/**/*_manifest.json
!data/**/.gitkeep

# Figures and results ARE committed: they are the artefact.
!figures/*.png
!results/*.json

# Reduced runs live here, in their own directory, so a smoke run can never be
# read as a stage's record: the directory is the separation. They are committed
# anyway, because a smoke run that disagrees with the full one is the thing you
# want in the history rather than out of it.
!results/subset/*.json

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Superseded pre-registrations and fixtures. This repository does not delete:
# a recursive delete once destroyed hours of retrieval, so anything no longer
# read is renamed with this suffix and left where it is.
*.expired
*.expired[0-9]
# Dated variant, which the fingerprints arm already uses:
# <name>.expired_<yyyymmdd>_pre_<tag>. Added 2026-08-15 after two A7
# backups sat in the untracked list waiting to be committed by accident.
*.expired_*

# Prepared commit messages, not part of the repository.
COMMIT_MSG*.txt

# Git scratch for a single stage: prepared add-lists and how-to notes, written
# for one commit and not part of the repository. COMMIT_MSG*.txt and HANDOFF*.md
# were already excluded and these were not, so `git add -A` would have swept
# them in. Found 2026-08-18 while auditing what an outside reader would see.
GIT_HOWTO*.md
GIT_ADD*.txt
GIT_REWRITE*
b8_paths.txt

# Retired out of the repository rather than deleted, because this repository
# does not delete. Nothing here is on any code path.
_to_delete/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-stage exclusions. Read this before adding one.
#
# The test is a PROPERTY OF THE FILE, never a state of the stage. "This stage
# has not closed yet", "its register is held elsewhere", "it has no section in
# RESULTS.md" are all states, and states go stale while the rule that quotes
# them does not. Whoever reads such a rule later cannot tell whether it still
# holds without re-deriving it, which is the cost this paragraph exists to
# prevent.
#
# That is not hypothetical. A rule here once kept an entire stage's code and
# records out on the ground that it had no section in RESULTS.md. It then
# closed and reported 422 marker rows across 227 issuers in RESULTS.md, and the
# rule went on excluding the very script that produced those numbers, because
# nothing makes a rule notice that its premise expired. Removed 2026-08-22
# after re-deriving it by hand: the second time anyone had to.
#
# An unfinished stage is not a reason to exclude anything. Its records ship
# carrying `diagnostic_only` and a `diagnostic_reason` that says in plain words
# which readings are not yet the stage's own. That is the mechanism for
# incompleteness, and it is already running.
#
# So a rule below is well formed only if it names a file that is not a stage's
# reading and never will be: a hand-made backup, a subset run, a scratch file,
# a cache that rebuilds from raw. If the reason cannot be written without
# describing what some stage is currently doing, the rule is the wrong shape.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# B10. Never the stage's reading, by construction rather than by timing. The
# first rule catches the hand-made backups taken before a mechanism changed;
# the second and third catch subset runs, whose file names carry the vintages
# they cover, so their numbers answer a narrower question than the stage's.
results/b10_*.json.*
results/b10_*.pre*.json
results/b10_*.[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]*.json

# B14 的派生面板缓存（data/cache/b14/panel_*.csv，约 60 MB）。
# 与 data/raw/* 同理：可从原始 .gzip 两分钟重建，不进仓库。
# 重建：python experiments/b14_tickpilot_panel.py --build
data/cache/

# B8 打包器的逐步日志。它们是一次运行的痕迹，不是产物：
# 重跑即覆盖，且内容里带机器与时长。产物是 results/b8_*.md 与 b8_verdicts.json。
results/_b8_package_log/

# Rule 19's baseline: a copy of the records taken before a shared module
# is touched, so that a later diff has something to diff against. Working
# state, not an artefact.
results/_baseline/
results/_baseline.expired_*/

# Column caches keyed on the retrieval's file list. A stage that reads two
# thousand raw files writes the columns it needs here once, so a rerun is a
# load rather than a second pass; the cache is a function of files that
# data/raw/* already excludes, and it is invalidated and rebuilt when that file
# list changes rather than being trusted across retrievals. Same reason as
# data/cache/ above, different directory because these are keyed per stage.
# Currently holds B2c's 800 MB column store, which is past GitHub's own
# per-file limit, and A2e's.
results/CACHE/

# B35: Census API key, never committed
data/b35/census_key.txt
**/census_key.txt

# B41: raw API responses cached per query. Same reason as data/cache/ above,
# different directory because these are keyed per report and query rather than
# per stage. The two small readings beside it, structure.json and
# earliest.json, are evidence and do belong in the repository.
data/b41/cache/
data/b41/**/*.part
data/b41/**/*.corrupt.*.json

# B41 and B35 share the Market News key. It lives beside the repository rather
# than inside it, but these patterns are here so that a copy dropped in by
# accident cannot be committed. Same intent as census_key.txt above.
.mars_api_key
**/.mars_api_key
**/mars_api_key*

# B41-5 pulls the fullness series from NASS Quick Stats. Same shape as the
# Market News key above: the key lives beside the repository, the raw responses
# cache under data/, and the small derived reading is what belongs here.
data/b41/nass_cache/
.nass_api_key
**/.nass_api_key
**/nass_api_key*

# B42: the daily deliverable-under-registration and weekly stocks workbooks.
# Both are published as the current issue only, so this cache is the series and
# it is not reproducible by re-running anything. It is data, and data stays on
# the machine that fetched it.
data/b42/

# B35: the AMS report catalogue, one cached API response. Same reason as
# data/b41/cache/ above: reproducible from a single request with a key, and
# data stays on the machine that fetched it.
data/b35/catalogue.json
data/b35/*.corrupt.json

# Agmarknet 逐日到货面板（第三方抓取件，github.com/iancovert/Agmarknet）
# 视同不可再生（第 6 条），不进仓库（11·2 第 6 类）
data/agmark/

# B34: the LFS quarters and every cache derived from them. These are End User
# Licence microdata from the UK Data Service, individual level records, and the
# licence does not permit redistribution. The raw .dta files sit under
# data/raw/ which is already excluded, but the extracted per-person cache lives
# here, so it needs its own rule. data/SOURCES.md records where to get the
# originals and on what basis.
data/b34/

# B30-16, B30-17, B30-18. The licence is not what excludes these. DB1B and the
# Consumer Airfare Report are Bureau of Transportation Statistics output and the
# CMT curve is Treasury output; both are works of the US government and carry no
# copyright there, and neither agency attaches a reuse condition. SOFR and EFFR
# are New York Fed content, whose terms of use permit copying and distributing
# in any format, and permit derived works, on three conditions: carry the source
# identifier and copyright notice, do not imply endorsement, and do not impose
# more restrictive terms. data/SOURCES.md carries that notice.
#
# What excludes them is the rule at the top of this file, that raw data is not
# redistributed, plus 315 MB of DB1B quarters that a documented fetch rebuilds.
#
# data/*/raw/ generalises the data/raw/* line above, which only ever matched the
# top level directory. On disk that pattern covers exactly b30_16 and b30_17; no
# other station keeps a raw/ subdirectory, so it widens the rule without
# changing what any other station does.
data/*/raw/

# data/raw as a bare line was tried on 2026-09-06 and withdrawn the same day.
# It excludes the directory itself, and git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so the manifest exception above stops being evaluated at all and
# every manifest under data/raw goes with it. That is also why the !data/**/
# line near the top exists: it re-admits directories so the deep exceptions can
# run. The rule that was actually needed is narrower and is the next two lines.
#
# Two third-party repositories were cloned under data/raw. Git records an
# embedded repository as a gitlink, a directory-shaped entry, so !data/**/
# re-admits it where data/** alone would have caught it. Naming the two closes
# that hole without touching anything else. What each one is and where it came
# from is in data/SOURCES.md; neither is redistributed here.
data/raw/gaokao/Gaokao-Compass-11M/
data/raw/havana_lob/
data/b30_18/

# Derived cell matrices keyed by a config hash, one per source-quarter-config,
# rebuilt from the raw quarters above in one run. Same class as data/cache/ and
# data/b41/cache/. The readings beside them stay: the stage*.json files are the
# artefact, and so are the small *_diag.json files, which record the shape of
# each cell matrix and are the only provenance a reader gets for it.
results/b30_16/cell_*.csv.gz
results/b30_17/mat_*.csv.gz
